#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/language/plurals.rst:3
msgid "Plurals"
msgstr "Flertalsformer"

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/language/plurals.rst:6
msgid "Short Example"
msgstr "Kort eksempel"

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/language/plurals.rst:8
msgid "The english language is very simple when it comes to plurals:"
msgstr ""
"Det engelske sprog er meget simpelt, når det kommer til flertalsformer:"

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/language/plurals.rst:10
msgid "*You have 0 elephants, 1 elephant, or 2+ elephants.*"
msgstr "*Du har 0 elefanter, 1 elefant, eller 2+ elefanter.*"

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/language/plurals.rst:12
msgid "So basically you have 2 different forms: one singular and one plural."
msgstr "Så grundlæggende har du 2 forskellige former: én ental og én flertal."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/language/plurals.rst:15
msgid ""
"But for some other languages this is quite a bit more difficult. Let's take "
"the Bosnian language as another example:"
msgstr ""
"Men for nogle andre sprog er dette en del mere vanskeligt. Lad os tage det "
"bosniske sprog som et andet eksempel:"

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/language/plurals.rst:18
msgid ""
"*You have [1/21/31] slon, [2/3/4] slona, [0/5/6] slonova and [7/8/9/11] ...*"
msgstr ""
"*Du har [1/21/31] slon, [2/3/4] slona, [0/5/6] slonova og [7/8/9/11] ...*"

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/language/plurals.rst:20
msgid ""
"The problem with the old system of plurals was that you would have needed to"
" specify them all, and get a loop in there."
msgstr ""
"Problemet med det gamle system til flertalsformer var, at du skulle angive "
"dem alle og have en løkke ind i det."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/language/plurals.rst:24
msgid ""
"As we are not the first developers facing this problem, it was not really "
"hard to find a suitable solution. We decided to use the system from "
"`Unicode.org`_, which is e.g. used by Mozilla."
msgstr ""
"Da vi ikke er de første udviklere, der står over for dette problem, var det "
"ikke rigtig svært at finde en passende løsning. Vi besluttede at bruge "
"systemet fra `Unicode.org`_, som f.eks. bruges af Mozilla."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/language/plurals.rst:29
msgid "Plural Rules"
msgstr "Flertalsregler"

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/language/plurals.rst:30
msgid ""
"So we defined the following 16 rules for plurals. First point is the "
"language family, afterwards there are a number of rows with the following "
"format: **<key> - <rule>: <example-numbers>**"
msgstr ""
"Så vi definerede følgende 16 regler for flertalsformer. Det første punkt er "
"sprogfamilien, derefter er der en række rækker med følgende format: "
"**<nøgle> - <regel>: <eksempeltal>**"

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/language/plurals.rst:36
msgid ""
"0 is handled as a special case. If you add a key 0 to your array, that will "
"be used in case of 0 independent of the plural rule."
msgstr ""
"Nul (0) behandles som et specialtilfælde. Hvis du tilføjer en nøgle 0 til "
"dit array, vil den blive brugt i tilfælde af 0 uafhængigt af flertalsreglen."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/language/plurals.rst:40
msgid "Rule #0"
msgstr "Regel #0"

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/language/plurals.rst:41
msgid ""
"Families: Asian (Chinese, Japanese, Korean, Vietnamese), Persian, "
"Turkic/Altaic (Turkish), Thai, Lao"
msgstr ""
"Familier: Asiatisk (kinesisk, japansk, koreansk, vietnamesisk), persisk, "
"tyrkisk/altaisk (tyrkisk), thai, lao"

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/language/plurals.rst:42
msgid "1 - everything: 0, 1, 2, ..."
msgstr "1 - alt: 0, 1, 2, ..."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/language/plurals.rst:45
msgid "Rule #1"
msgstr "Regel #1"

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/language/plurals.rst:46
msgid ""
"Families: Germanic (Danish, Dutch, English, Faroese, Frisian, German, "
"Norwegian, Swedish), Finno-Ugric (Estonian, Finnish, Hungarian), Language "
"isolate (Basque), Latin/Greek (Greek), Semitic (Hebrew), Romanic (Italian, "
"Portuguese, Spanish, Catalan)"
msgstr ""
"Familier: Germansk (dansk, hollandsk, engelsk, færøsk, frisisk, tysk, norsk,"
" svensk), finsk-ugrisk (estisk, finsk, ungarsk), sprogisolat (baskisk), "
"latinsk/græsk (græsk), semitisk (hebraisk), romansk (italiensk, portugisisk,"
" spansk, catalansk)"

